Leo Nitsche wrote:
> Hi all,
> 
> 
> I'm wondernig about what is the more relevant package among limma and
> Beadarray to analyse data from Illumina beadchip microarrays?

The two packages do different things; beadarray is for preprocessing the 
raw data and limma is for fitting linear models and detecting 
differentially expressed genes. So both are relevant, just at different 
stages of the game.

