I think this is pointing to an issue with your R installation per se; it
thinks that it will link to a system-supplied liblapack, but cannot find
one. It would have decided or been told to use a system-supplied lapack
when R was configured and installed. It might be that there is a
liblapack available

  % locate liblapack

and if so your system can be configured to find it (details of
configuring your system are best delegated to your local sys. admin if
this is mostly gibberish to you). I think that someone would have fairly
deliberately had to set lapack to liblapack, rather than using R's
buiilt-in libRlapack.

Martin

